@kem-a  To write to /opt, you need root privileges. Unless you create a directory where you can only read/write once and move all the AppImages there, it would be a mess, even with updates.

When delta updates are performed, a new temporary file is created next to the AppImage until the update is complete.

It would therefore be necessary to create a writable directory in /opt.

@HaleTom However, for backup purposes, it's best to save everything in $HOME, or at least in a directory where you can write without necessarily having to use root privileges.

@Bl4ckspell7 thank you for reporting. Two things:

1. in update field you entered Android repo address: `https://github.com/ente-io/ente` ≠ `https://github.com/ente-io/photos-desktop`. Putting correct update link will fix your issue

2. app should not try to update when wrong repo is entered. That is a bug

@probonopd what system is it? 

It is unlikely this is an AppManager issue and something deeper with GTK.

The good news is that I can add a fix myself in `quick-sharun`, I actually want to start making it possible to run applications without dbus at all.
